WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
A ticker. A question. A bigger picture.
Stockbear: a focused market-research project. Real UI captures; formula-generated data.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Start with what matters.
A sortable watchlist leads directly into native AAPL ticker research.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.400
Change the question of time.
One year of generated synthetic history.

4
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.733
Choose a range.
The actual chart switches to three months.

5
00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:19.200
A shared benchmark.
AAPL and SPY relative returns on common generated dates.

6
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.000
Daily to weekly.
Change resolution using native chart controls.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The number is only half the story.
Return, SPY excess,20-session volatility and maximum drawdown with calculation notes. Historical descriptions, not forecasts.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Different symbols. Common ground.
AAPL, MSFT and SPY comparison uses common observation dates and request-driven server rendering.

9
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Three paths. One deliberate experience.
Editorial architecture: ISR renders watchlist/curated tickers ahead; SSR answers selected-symbol requests; client controls refresh without losing context. This is not app UI.

10
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Measure. Don't mythologize.
Native freshness timestamps and Browser Performance API diagnostics. Local observations, not production benchmarks.

11
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Research, thoughtfully rendered.
Stockbear: a project in data, interaction and delivery. Next.js and TypeScript.
